{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.MvPolynomialHeight","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.MvPolynomialHeight","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.CommRing","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Abs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Int","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Int.Units","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_det_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_det_le","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvPolynomialHeight.lean#L159-L192","doc":"**`H(det M) ≤ m! · (S·B)^m`** for an `m × m` matrix of integer multivariate polynomials\nwith entries of support size at most `S` and height at most `B`.\n\nLeibniz expands the determinant into `m!` signed products of `m` entries.  The sign is a unit\nof `ℤ`, so it does not move the absolute value at all; each product is bounded by\n`abs_coeff_prod_le`; and the `m!` is just the number of permutations.\n\nThis is what turns a height bound on an auxiliary polynomial into one on a generalized\nWronskian.  ⚠ It needs `S` — a *support-size* bound on the entries — not only a height bound;\nsupplying that for iterated `pderiv`s is `card_support_pderiv_le` in\n`QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_prod_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_prod_le","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvPolynomialHeight.lean#L140-L157","doc":"**`H(∏_{i ∈ s} Fᵢ) ≤ (S·B)^{#s}`** — the `Finset` form of the previous theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_multiset_prod_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_multiset_prod_le","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvPolynomialHeight.lean#L103-L138","doc":"**`H(∏ t) ≤ (S·B)^{card t}`** for a multiset of factors, each of support size at most `S`\nand height at most `B`.\n\n`1 ≤ S` is what lets the bound be stated as a clean `k`-th power.  The sharp form shaves one\n`S` — the recursion only ever applies `abs_coeff_mul_le` with an *original* factor in the\nfirst slot, never a partial product, so the last factor contributes no support cost — but\ncarrying `S^{k-1}` through the induction costs more than it buys. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_mul_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_mul_le","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvPolynomialHeight.lean#L56-L101","doc":"**`H(f·g) ≤ #supp(f) · H(f) · H(g)`.**\n\nIn `coeff n (f·g) = ∑ coeff a f · coeff b g` over the antidiagonal of `n`, a summand survives\nonly when `a ∈ supp f`, and `b = n − a` is then determined — so at most `#supp f` terms\nsurvive, each bounded by `H(f)·H(g)`.\n\n⚠ The easy direction.  See the module header. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_one_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_one_le","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvPolynomialHeight.lean#L50-L54","doc":"`H(1) ≤ 1`: the base case of the product induction. ","signatureChunk":0}]}